{
  "format_version": 1,
  "_comment": [
    "WHO YOU ARE, for any tool that needs to know and must not hardcode it.",
    "FILL THIS IN before the first commit from any repo that resolves this",
    "set -- bootstrap cannot know who you are, so it ships the placeholders",
    "below and precedent_bootstrap_source.py's verify() reports the file as",
    "unfinished until they are replaced.",
    "",
    "WHAT READS IT. BestPractice's commit-identity.sh SessionStart hook is",
    "installed into SHARED repositories, which deliberately name no person.",
    "It resolves your individual source -- from this repo's own root when it",
    "IS that source, otherwise from the path ~/.config/precedent/config.json",
    "names -- and reads this file. That is how a shared repo gets your name,",
    "your address and your timezone without carrying any of them in its own",
    "tracked files.",
    "",
    "THE TIMEZONE IS THE HALF PEOPLE MISS. The hook only ENFORCES an",
    "author-date offset that somebody actually declared; a timezone it had",
    "to guess earns a warning and nothing more. So an unfilled `timezone`",
    "here does not fail loudly -- it silently downgrades the check to a",
    "guess, and wrong-offset commits reach the remote before anyone notices.",
    "Three such incidents in two days prompted this file being shipped at",
    "all (BestPractice AGENTS.md's gotchas, 2026-09-07 and 2026-09-08).",
    "",
    "Use an IANA zone name (`America/New_York`, `Europe/Berlin`),",
    "never an offset like `-05:00` -- git resolves the",
    "offset from the zone at commit time, which is what makes daylight",
    "saving handle itself.",
    "",
    "PRONOUNS ARE THE SAME SHAPE AS THE TIMEZONE, and are here for the same",
    "reason: they are a fact about a person, and a shared repository that",
    "deliberately names nobody has no way to know them and no business",
    "asserting one. Write them as the pair a session would actually use in a",
    "sentence -- `he/him`, `she/her`, `they/them` -- and nothing else: this",
    "field declares how to REFER to you, not your gender, which nothing here",
    "reads and nothing here should store.",
    "",
    "WHAT READS IT: a session, when it writes about you in the third person.",
    "No tool enforces it, exactly as no tool enforces `register` -- the value",
    "is declared here and the practice `declared-pronouns` (BestPractice",
    "universal) says what follows from it. Leave it unfilled and that",
    "practice falls back to `they/them` for you, which is safe and is not",
    "what you asked for.",
    "",
    "REGISTER IS THE THIRD FACT OF THE SAME SHAPE: how technical a reply to",
    "you should be. It is yours to declare, because nothing else can tell --",
    "there is no field anywhere that says what kind of person you are, on",
    "purpose (practice: technical-describes-people). Write it as one plain",
    "sentence a session can follow: `somewhat technical: I read code and",
    "want the real name for a thing, glossed once`, or `not technical: say",
    "what it means for my document, never what the tool did`, or anything",
    "in between, in your own words.",
    "",
    "WHAT READS IT: a session, when it writes to you. Leave it unfilled and",
    "a team-level default may apply -- one team here falls back to writing",
    "for a reader who is not technical -- which is safe and may not be what",
    "you wanted. Added to the skeleton 2026-09-14; a set built before then",
    "has no key at all, and `--verify` names the absent key."
  ],
  "name": "{{PERSON_NAME}}",
  "email": "{{PERSON_EMAIL}}",
  "timezone": "{{PERSON_TIMEZONE}}",
  "pronouns": "{{PERSON_PRONOUNS}}",
  "register": "{{PERSON_REGISTER}}",
  "ci_every_hours": 0,
  "_ci_every_hours_comment": [
    "HOW OFTEN GITHUB ACTIONS RUNS IN YOUR PRIVATE REPOS. 0, the default,",
    "means every push, exactly as if this key were absent. A number above 0",
    "means at most once every that many hours: commit-identity.sh's commit",
    "hook adds [skip ci] to a commit on a private repo's primary branch when",
    "CI already ran there more recently than that, so GitHub never starts a",
    "runner and bills nothing. Public repos, feature branches and anything",
    "the hook is unsure of always run CI. A repo overrides this for itself",
    "with its own `ci_every_hours` in precedent.json -- a practice set that",
    "other repos read from should declare 0 there.",
    "",
    "Your local deep check stays the real gate; CI becomes the backstop.",
    "Full design: BestPractice spec/CI_CADENCE_PLAN.md."
  ],
  "relayed_authorization": "refused",
  "_relayed_authorization_comment": [
    "DOES YOUR APPROVAL TRAVEL? When work you authorized has to be finished",
    "in a session you are not typing in -- the usual cause is a repository",
    "this session cannot reach -- the session holding your words relays them",
    "to one that can. The receiving session cannot tell a true relay from a",
    "fabricated one, so unless you say otherwise here it stops at the pull",
    "request and you approve again, in that other window.",
    "",
    "Set this to \"accepted\" and it merges on the relay instead. What it",
    "may then do is still bounded: the named work only, the destination",
    "repository's own routine branch, that repository's checks passing, and",
    "nothing that repository protects -- a branch behind review, or a merge",
    "it requires a named person to approve, still requires that person.",
    "",
    "THE TRADE, so you are choosing it rather than discovering it: with",
    "\"accepted\", anything that can deliver a message into a session holding",
    "your sources can cause a merge within those bounds. With \"refused\" --",
    "the default, and what an absent field means -- every cross-repository",
    "handoff costs you a second approval in a second window.",
    "",
    "Revoke by editing this line; nothing expires on its own. The practice",
    "is `relayed-authorization` (BestPractice universal), and",
    "`python3 tools/precedent_identity.py --relay` is what reads it."
  ],
  "ci_workflows": "disabled",
  "_ci_workflows_comment": [
    "SHOULD `precedent_install.py` WRITE THE GITHUB ACTIONS WORKFLOW into a",
    "dependent repository at install time? GitHub Actions minutes are",
    "metered per PRIVATE repository and billed per run, rounded up to the",
    "minute -- so vendoring Precedent into many private repos, saving the",
    "way a save button gets used, means paying for a workflow run on every",
    "one of those saves, whether you wanted the check or not.",
    "",
    "\"disabled\" is the value here AND the engine's own default when this",
    "field is absent (practice: declared-default-is-applied) -- most people",
    "reading this have the same minutes limit everyone else on a plan does,",
    "so the installer does not spend it for you unasked. Set it to",
    "\"enabled\" and future installs write the workflow again, unchanged.",
    "",
    "THIS ONLY CONTROLS THE INSTALLER'S DEFAULT. You can still copy",
    "templates/github-actions/doc-lint.yml.template into any one repo by",
    "hand, any time, whatever this says -- it is the STARTING behavior for",
    "a fresh `precedent_install.py` run, not a lock. And a repo where you",
    "push to the default branch very frequently has a lower-cost variant,",
    "templates/github-actions/doc-lint-scheduled.yml.template, that trades",
    "per-push billing for a fixed cadence -- this field does not choose",
    "between the two; GITHUB_ACTIONS.md does.",
    "",
    "WHAT READS IT: tools/precedent_identity.py's ci_preference(), called by",
    "tools/precedent_install.py's _bootstrap_and_ci(). Added 2026-09-15,",
    "raised by the person paying for it: \"I think it should be disabled BY",
    "DEFAULT because most people will have limits like mine.\""
  ],
  "grandfathered_commit_shas": [],
  "_grandfathered_comment": [
    "Commits exempted from the identity and timezone checks that share this",
    "one list. Every entry is an object with a `sha` and a `note` saying why.",
    "",
    "It is for commits ALREADY PUBLISHED when the violation surfaced, where",
    "rewriting history would cost more than the wrong value does (practice:",
    "no-rewrite-for-warnings). It is never a way to skip setting the identity",
    "or the timezone correctly in the first place: an unpushed commit gets",
    "fixed, not listed. An exemption with no note is the silence these checks",
    "exist to replace -- keep it empty until you genuinely need one."
  ]
}
